    "title": "6-month-old boy found dead in NYC home: cops - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By David DeTurris ,\n10 hours ago\nA 6-month-old boy was found dead in Brooklyn early Wednesday, cops said.\nThe unresponsive newborn was found just after midnight in a home near Flatlands Avenue and East 99th Street in Canarsie, police said.\nKentucky child killer who stabbed sleeping boy to death released from prison as father slams judicial system\nEMS rushed the baby to Brookdale University Hospital Medical Center, where he was pronounced dead, according to authorities.\nFlorida dad kills infant son with leafblower — allegedly claiming he thought it would be fun\nThe unresponsive newborn was found just after midnight in a home near Flatlands Ave. and E 99th St. in Canarsie, police said. Kyle Mazza/Shutterstock EMS rushed the baby to Brookdale University Hospital Medical Center, where he was pronounced dead, according to authorities. Kyle Mazza/Shutterstock CLICK HERE TO SIGN UP FOR OUR MORNING REPORT NEWSLETTER\nSources said that the infant was found with no signs of trauma.\nPolice were investigating whether the child’s death was criminal.\nThe Office of the Medical Examiner will probe the cause of death.\nFor the latest metro stories, top headlines, breaking news and more, visit nypost.com/metro/\n17",
    "summary": "The unresponsive newborn was found just after midnight in a home near Flatlands Avenue and East 99th Street in Canarsie, police said. Kentucky child killer who stabbed sleeping boy to death released from prison as father slams judicial system EMS rushed the baby to Brookdale University Hospital Medical Center, where he was pronounced dead, according to authorities. Florida dad kills infant son with leafblower — allegedly claiming he thought it would be fun The unresponsive newborn was found just after midnight in a home near Flatlands Ave. and E 99th St. in Canarsie, police said.",
